      "message": "This is a pretty unusual constructor to call (I think?).\n\nIf I\u0027m understanding this correctly, you are creating a shared pointer with an empty deleter. So when the reference count gets to 0, it won\u0027t clean up any memory?\n\nIs that because it is starting with a reference, and the class that called this parse method and passed in its Service object is going to continue to own the storage?\n\nIn that case, couldn\u0027t all the shared_ptr\u003cService\u003e instances be replaced by Service\u0026?\n\nIt is valid to have a class data member that is a reference. You just have to immediately assign it a value in the constructor initialization list.\n\nSorry if I\u0027m misunderstanding this.",
